### Creating Texture from TextureSource with Rectangle Frame

Source: https://github.com/pixijs/pixijs/blob/dev/src/spritesheet/Spritesheet.ts

Create a new Texture from an existing texture source (TextureSource) with a Rectangle frame for spritesheet cropping. The frame defines which region of the source to display, and orig/trim define the original and trimmed boundaries. These textures can be used as AnimatedSprite frames.

```typescript
this.textures[i] = new Texture({
    source: this.textureSource,
    frame,
    orig,
    trim,
    rotate: data.rotated ? 2 : 0,
    defaultAnchor: data.anchor,
    defaultBorders: data.borders,
    label: i.toString(),
});
```

--------------------------------

### Frame Rectangle Creation for Spritesheet Parsing

Source: https://github.com/pixijs/pixijs/blob/dev/src/spritesheet/Spritesheet.ts

How to create Rectangle objects for frame, orig, and trim when parsing spritesheet data. The frame Rectangle specifies the position (x,y) and dimensions (w,h) of the sprite within the texture source, while orig defines the original source dimensions.

```typescript
const frame = new Rectangle(
    Math.floor(rect.x) / this.resolution,
    Math.floor(rect.y) / this.resolution,
    Math.floor(rect.w) / this.resolution,
    Math.floor(rect.h) / this.resolution
);

const orig = new Rectangle(
    0,
    0,
    Math.floor(sourceSize.w) / this.resolution,
    Math.floor(sourceSize.h) / this.resolution
);
```

--------------------------------

### Creating AnimatedSprite with array of Textures and setting animation properties

Source: https://github.com/pixijs/pixijs/blob/dev/examples/animated-sprite_animation.ts

This example demonstrates the official API pattern for creating an AnimatedSprite from an array of Textures, setting animationSpeed, anchor, scale, and calling play() to start the animation.

```typescript
// Create an array to store the textures
const textures = [];
let i;

for (i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
  const framekey = `0123456789 ${i}.ase`;
  const texture = Texture.from(framekey);
  const time = spritesheet.data.frames[framekey].duration;

  textures.push({ texture, time });
}

const scaling = 4;

// Create a slow AnimatedSprite
const slow = new AnimatedSprite(textures);

slow.anchor.set(0.5);
slow.scale.set(scaling);
slow.animationSpeed = 0.5;
slow.x = (app.screen.width - slow.width) / 2;
slow.y = app.screen.height / 2;
slow.play();
app.stage.addChild(slow);
```

